ences, traditional practices and customs are often replaced by more mainstream ideals. This can lead to a loss of unique cultural identities, as societies seek to conform to global norms. On the other hand, globalization also provides opportunities for cultural exchange and enrichment. Through the sharing of ideas and experiences, different cultures can learn from one another and create a more diverse and inclusive global society. This can lead to the formation of hybrid cultures, where traditional practices are merged with new ideas from different parts of the world. In conclusion, globalization has both positive and negative effects on cultural identity. While it can lead to homogenization, it also offers opportunities for cultural exchange and diversity. It is essential for societies to find a balance between embracing global influences and preserving their cultural heritage. By doing so, we can create a world that celebrates both unity and diversity.", "encoded_message": "Worldwide integration together with Civilizational Selfhood. Worldwide integration includes experienced an deep influence upon Ethnic selfhood throughout the earth. Considering land transform into further tied across progress in terms of science as well as intensified commerce, the dissemination of theories, morals, plus routines contains turn into additionally pervasive. Although Internationalization contains certainly favored populations within multiple means, it features too lifted worries pertaining to the safeguarding of Social character. An individual of the principal consequences of Globalism upon Civilizational personality amounts to the uniformity of societies. Because people are exposed to different cultural influences, traditional practices and customs are often replaced by more mainstream ideals. This can lead to a loss of unique cultural identities, as societies seek to conform to global norms. On the other hand, globalization also provides opportunities for cultural exchange and e